SYNTHESIS
  The two-far actual-boundary deviation has only four live before-depths: 1,2,5,6.
  Depths 3 and 4 are exactly silent because C(t), C(t-1), and C(t-2) all equal 1.
  Therefore the two-far proof can ignore the bulk middle mass after the boundary step.
  The remaining analytic lemma is a signed four-depth kernel bound, not a seven-depth bound.
